Watch Out for These Fees
Before choosing a checking account, know the common fees that can quietly cost you:
    • Monthly maintenance fees – often waived with direct deposit or a minimum balance 
    • Overdraft fees – can run $25–$35 per occurrence 
    • ATM fees – add up fast if you use out-of-network machines 
    • Low balance fees – charged if your account dips below a set minimum 
A good account should offer simple ways to avoid these costs altogether.

Features That Actually Matter
Beyond avoiding fees, the best accounts offer:
    • Mobile banking – check deposit, bill pay, and instant alerts 
